# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The model chain. Tried top to bottom until one answers; a tier is skipped
# entirely when its key is absent, so one key on its own is a valid setup.
#
# Capture makes many small model calls — every capture sorts, every thread
# update re-summarises, every edit is proofread — so the fastest free tiers
# come first. If every tier fails, the app still keeps the capture — saved
# verbatim and flagged unsorted, to be sorted later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Groq. https://console.groq.com/keys — very fast, generous free tier.
#    Daily free tokens reset on their own; a spent day just falls through
#    to the next tier.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# 2. Mistral. https://console.mistral.ai — useful fast fallback once a key is
#    configured. Accounts and model access can vary, so test the key directly
#    before relying on it in production.
#    Rate limits can be strict (429 + Retry-After when hit) —
#    the app's fail-fast chain just falls through to Gemini meanwhile.
#    mistral-small-latest is the fast workhorse; swap MISTRAL_MODEL if a
#    better fit shows up.
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
# MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-small-latest

# 3. Google AI Studio. https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — a plain AIza...
#    string. Not an OAuth client id/secret: those sign users into Google
#    accounts and cannot authenticate Gemini calls. Reliable free tier;
#    kept as the quality fallback behind the two fast tiers.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# 4. OpenRouter. https://openrouter.ai/keys — last resort. Its free models
#    share tight rate limits, so it only catches what the tiers above miss.
#    The default is a :free model; set OPENROUTER_MODEL to any paid slug it
#    lists only if the account is intentionally funded.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b:free

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-user password gate. Leave unset and the gate is off, which is fine
# locally. Set it in production — an open /api/sort spends someone's quota.
# The login endpoint rate-limits by client address and the model endpoints by
# address too. Both read the caller's real IP from cf-connecting-ip /
# x-real-ip / the rightmost x-forwarded-for entry. On a bare Node host with
# no proxy in front, an attacker can forge that header, so put nginx or
# Cloudflare in front before relying on the limits.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rate limits — deployment protections, not user throttles. The real quota
# owner is the model provider, so a local single-user install needs none of
# these; set any to 0 to turn it off. Leave them at the defaults when
# hosting where strangers could reach the instance.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CAPTURE_MODEL_LIMIT=40        # model calls per client per minute
# CAPTURE_TTS_LIMIT=120         # speech-synthesis requests per minute
# CAPTURE_SYNC_LIMIT=60         # hub pulls/pushes per client per minute
# CAPTURE_LOGIN_LIMIT=5         # login attempts per client per 15 min

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: the human-sounding voice.
#
# Spoken replies in Distill try three engines in order: Kokoro (TTS_URL,
# near-human, runs on your Mac), then the Microsoft Edge neural voice
# (keyless, server-side, human-sounding), then the browser's built-in voice
# as the last resort. Set TTS_URL to a running Kokoro server (see SETUP.md)
# and the app switches to it automatically. Leave it unset and replies use
# the Edge neural voice — still human-sounding, and it works everywhere.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TTS_URL=http://localhost:8880/v1
# TTS_VOICE=af_bella
# EDGE_TTS_VOICE=en-US-AriaNeural
